---
import BaseLayout from '@/layouts/BaseLayout.astro';

const h2 = 'font-display text-2xl font-bold text-warm-900 mt-12 mb-4';
const p = 'text-warm-700 leading-relaxed mb-5';
const link = 'underline underline-offset-2 decoration-warm-400 hover:decoration-warm-900';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy"
  description="What this site and the Basketball Video Analyzer app collect: cookieless visit counts on the site, and nothing from the app unless you send feedback."
>
  <article class="py-20 sm:py-28">
    <div class="max-w-6xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
      <div class="max-w-xl">
        <h1 class="font-display text-4xl sm:text-5xl font-bold text-warm-900 leading-[1.1] mb-6">Privacy</h1>
        <p class="text-lg text-warm-700 mb-12">
          This site sets no cookies and stores nothing in your browser.
          Updated 16 November 2026.
        </p>

        <h2 class={h2}>On this website</h2>
        <p class={p}>
          Two tools count visits, and neither stores anything in your browser.
        </p>
        <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-3 text-warm-700 leading-relaxed mb-5">
          <li>
            <strong class="text-warm-900">Vercel Web Analytics</strong> records the page, the referring site, your
            country, and your browser and device type. It recognises a visit by a hash of the request that is
            thrown away after 24 hours. <a class={link} href="https://vercel.com/docs/analytics/privacy-policy" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Vercel's details</a>.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong class="text-warm-900">Google Analytics</strong> runs with storage turned off (consent mode,
            every type denied), so it sets no cookies and cannot tell one visit from the next. Google still
            receives each request, with its IP address and browser details, and counts page views and clicks on
            the download button from them.
          </li>
        </ul>
        <p class={p}>
          The site is hosted on Vercel behind Cloudflare, which keep the usual server logs (IP address, time, page)
          to run and protect the service.
        </p>

        <h2 class={h2}>In the app</h2>
        <p class={p}>
          The app has no account and no tracking. Your videos, clips and projects stay in folders on your computer.
          It connects to the internet only when it checks for an update, when you import a YouTube video, and when
          you send feedback.
        </p>
        <p class={p}>
          Feedback becomes a public issue on the app's GitHub repository, with your title and message plus the app
          version and operating system. Do not put anything in it you would not post publicly.
        </p>

        <h2 class={h2}>Questions</h2>
        <p class={p}>
          Open an issue on <a class={link} href="https://github.com/kauredo/basketball-video-analyzer/issues" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">GitHub</a>.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
